-- ============================================================================
-- seed_jobs_data.sql
--
-- Seeds 15 real job postings + their employer accounts + employer profiles.
--
-- DESIGNED TO RUN ON EVERY PIPELINE DEPLOYMENT, not just once. Every insert
-- uses ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, so running this 1 time or 100 times produces
-- the exact same end state — no duplicate-key errors, no duplicated rows.
--
-- IMPORTANT NOTES:
-- 1. This assumes schema.sql has already been run (tables exist).
-- 2. This deliberately EXCLUDES user IDs 11, 12, 13 (admin@portal.com,
--    student@portal.com, employer@portal.com) because those are already
--    seeded automatically by JobApplicationPortalApplication's
--    CommandLineRunner on every app startup. Do NOT add them here, or you
--    risk a duplicate-key conflict with the CommandLineRunner's own inserts.
-- 3. This also excludes job IDs 100, 201, 217 and their associated users/jobs
--    (test/placeholder data, not part of the real 15 JD set).
-- 4. All 15 employer accounts share a placeholder password hash and are NOT
--    intended to be logged into directly — they exist only so the JOBS
--    table's foreign key (EMPLOYER_USER_ID) has a valid row to point to.
-- 5. IDEMPOTENT BY DESIGN — every INSERT below uses ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING,
--    so this script is safe to run on EVERY pipeline deployment, not just
--    the first one. First run: inserts everything. Every run after that:
--    finds all 44 rows already exist (by primary key) and silently skips
--    them, leaving your data untouched. No errors, no duplicates, no
--    accidental resets of data students/employers may have since added.
-- ============================================================================

BEGIN;

